      en: "The Traditional Goat Farms of Brava are scattered across the island's rugged terrain. The local goat breed is hardy and adapted to arid conditions. Their milk is used to produce 'Queijo de Brava', a semi-hard cheese with a distinct flavor. Farms are small-scale, typically holding 20–50 goats. The goats graze freely on native shrubs. The cheese is aged for several months and is a prized local delicacy.",
